# BusyBox init on the RNS-E 192: the user interface (rnse-gui) on the
# screen's first console, a shell on the second (the GUI's "Shell" goes
# there; INFO comes back), typed on with the faceplate (docs/linux.md,
# "Rotary typing"), and a shell on the SH-4's serial port (the emulator
# prints it; no unit has it wired to anything known).
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS
tty1::respawn:/usr/bin/rnse-gui
tty2::respawn:-/bin/sh
ttySC1::respawn:-/bin/sh
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
